{{also|morgen}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈmɔɐ̯ɡŋ̩]|[ˈmɔɐ̯ɡən]|[ˈmɔʁɡŋ̩]|[ˈmɔʁɡən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Morgen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|morgen}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|morgan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*mr̥Hko||to blink, twinkle}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|Morgen}}, Dutch {{m|nl|morgen}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|moarn}}, English {{m|en|morn}}, {{m|en|morrow}}, Danish {{m|da|morgen}}, Swedish {{m|sv|morgon}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Morgens|Morgen|pl2=Morgende}}

# [[morning]]
# [[morgen]] (measure of land)

=====Usage notes=====
* The normal plural is unchanged '''''Morgen'''''.
* The plural ''Morgende'' is of dialectal origin. It is rather common colloquially but rarely used in literary German.

=====Declension=====
{{de-decl-noun-m|s||n}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|Vormittag}}
Usage notice: "Morgen" ist the day of the time when the sun rises, "Vormittag" the time between breakfast and lunch.

